        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: El Paso International Airport, Tucson International Airport, El Paso, Tucson, El Paso County, Pima County, Texas, Arizona, United States\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID\n- Concepts: public airports, joint civil-military airports, airport ownership, airport location\n\nFacts:\n- El Paso International Airport has IATA code ELP, ICAO code KELP, and FAA LID ELP.\n- El Paso International Airport is a public airport four miles northeast of downtown El Paso in El Paso County, Texas, United States.\n- Tucson International Airport has IATA code TUS, ICAO code KTUS, and FAA LID TUS.\n- Tucson International Airport is a public joint civil-military airport owned by the City of Tucson and located eight miles south of downtown Tucson in Pima County, Arizona.",
